@*
    Your half of the table: the hand, the question about it, and whether the computer is allowed
    to have an opinion.

    🔥 Everything drawn here came out of the SeatPrompt this seat was sent, through SeatBoard,
    and out of nothing else. There is no route from a component to the table session, which is
    what keeps ConcealmentTests standing in front of the page rather than beside it
    (BUILD-PLAN P13.4 acceptance 3).

    🔥 THE SEAT IS HANDED DOWN, NOT FETCHED (BUILD-PLAN P13.6). It used to be injected — one
    seat built when the table opened and shared by every circuit, which is right for solo play
    and wrong the moment two people are here. A SeatBoard belongs to a viewer, so the island
    that sat down owns it and this draws whichever one it was given.

    ⚠️ The hand comes first and the action bar last, which is the order they are on screen and
    the order they are read in (§3.11 B6). The question is answered by pressing a card as often
    as by pressing a button, so the cards must be above the bar and not below it.

    ⚠️ Subscribed here and unhooked in Dispose (§3.11 A5), and the re-render goes through
    InvokeAsync because the table speaks on the round's thread (§3.11 C15).
*@
@implements IDisposable

@if (_seat is not null)
{
    <section class="you @(_seat.IsYourTurn ? "asking" : null)" aria-labelledby="you-heading">
        <header class="head">
            <h2 id="you-heading">
                <span class="marker" aria-hidden="true">@(_seat.IsYourTurn ? "▶" : "·")</span>
                @_seat.Name
            </h2>

            <p class="hints">
                <input type="checkbox" id="show-hints" @bind="_hints" />
                <label for="show-hints">Hints</label>
            </p>
        </header>

        <HandPanel @ref="_hand"
                   Hand="_seat.Hand"
                   Hints="_hints"
                   Throwing="@(_seat.Asking?.Question == SeatQuestion.Discard)"
                   OnThrow="Throw" />

        <TurnPrompt @ref="_prompt" Asking="_seat.Asking" Hints="_hints" Names="Names" OnAnswer="Answer" />

        @*
            🔥 The sixth question, and the only one that is not about your hand (RULES.md §3
            step 2, §9 #45). It sits BESIDE the turn rather than inside TurnPrompt on purpose:
            every other question is put to one seat and answered privately, and this one is put
            to the whole table and every answer is said out loud.

            ⚠️ It is a standing answer, not a prompt. Somebody has to want the change and nobody
            may refuse it, so saying nothing is consent — which is why walking away never moves
            anybody's seat. The table is asked between deals, and asking clears what was said.

            ⚠️ Real controls, and the state is on the buttons rather than in prose (§3.11 A4):
            the one that is already your answer is disabled and says so with aria-pressed.
        *@
        <section class="seats" aria-labelledby="seats-heading">
            <h3 id="seats-heading">The seats</h3>

            <p class="said">@Said</p>

            <p class="asking">
                <button type="button" aria-pressed="@(_seat.Seating == SeatingOpinion.Ask)"
                        disabled="@(_seat.Seating == SeatingOpinion.Ask)"
                        @onclick="() => Say(SeatingOpinion.Ask)">Ask to change seats</button>

                <button type="button" aria-pressed="@(_seat.Seating == SeatingOpinion.Refuse)"
                        disabled="@(_seat.Seating == SeatingOpinion.Refuse)"
                        @onclick="() => Say(SeatingOpinion.Refuse)">Rather not</button>

                <button type="button" aria-pressed="@(_seat.Seating == SeatingOpinion.Consent)"
                        disabled="@(_seat.Seating == SeatingOpinion.Consent)"
                        @onclick="() => Say(SeatingOpinion.Consent)">Don't mind</button>
            </p>
        </section>
    </section>
}

@code {
    private SeatBoard? _seat;
    private TurnPrompt? _prompt;
    private HandPanel? _hand;
    private bool _hints = true;
    private bool _asked;
    private (int Round, int Turn, SeatQuestion Question)? _focused;

    /// <summary>
    /// Your own seat, or null when you came to watch.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// ⚠️ <b>It may change while this component lives</b> — a viewer who stood up and sat down
    /// again is handed a different one — so the subscription is made where the parameter is set
    /// and taken off the previous one first.
    /// </remarks>
    [Parameter]
    public SeatBoard? Seat { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Whether the computer's suggestions start switched on (the table's own setting).</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool Hints { get; set; } = true;

    /// <summary>
    /// What the seats are called, so a question about another player can name them.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// ⚠️ <b>Only one question is about another player</b> — the claim's permission (RULES.md
    /// §4.5) — and it names the seat that is asking. Handed down from the board like everything
    /// else on the page rather than looked up.
    /// </remarks>
    [Parameter]
    public IReadOnlyDictionary<PlayerId, string>? Names { get; set; }

    protected override void OnParametersSet()
    {
        if (!_asked)
        {
            _hints = Hints;
            _asked = true;
        }

        if (ReferenceEquals(_seat, Seat))
        {
            return;
        }

        Unhook();
        _seat = Seat;
        _focused = null;

        if (_seat is not null)
        {
            _seat.Changed += OnAsked;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// ✅ <b>§3.11 B7 — focus moves when the turn does.</b> When the table asks you something,
    /// focus lands on the first control of the prompt: the first button, or the first card in
    /// your hand when the question is which one to throw. Keyed on the question rather than on
    /// the render, so a bot's move somewhere else at the table never steals the caret.
    /// </summary>
    protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender)
    {
        if (_seat?.Asking is not { } asking)
        {
            _focused = null;
            return;
        }

        var now = (asking.Round, asking.TurnNumber, asking.Question);

        if (_focused == now)
        {
            return;
        }

        _focused = now;

        if (asking.Question == SeatQuestion.Discard)
        {
            if (_hand is not null)
            {
                await _hand.FocusAsync();
            }
        }
        else if (_prompt is not null)
        {
            await _prompt.FocusAsync();
        }
    }

    private void OnAsked() => _ = InvokeAsync(StateHasChanged);

    /// <remarks>
    /// A refused answer is not an error: the question stands and the seat has already said so,
    /// so there is nothing to do but let the next render draw what is really being asked (P13.2).
    /// </remarks>
    private void Answer(SeatAnswer answer) => _seat?.Answer(answer);

    private void Throw(Card card) => _seat?.Throw(card);

    /// <remarks>
    /// A refusal is not an error here either: a seat that has stood up says nothing, and the
    /// next render draws what it really said.
    /// </remarks>
    private void Say(SeatingOpinion opinion) => _seat?.Says(opinion);

    /// <summary>
    /// What this seat has said about the seating, in a sentence.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// ⚠️ <b>It says what happens next and not only what was pressed</b> (§3.11 C13): a control
    /// with a reason is the standard, and <em>consent</em> is the one answer whose meaning is not
    /// obvious from its own name — it is not a yes.
    /// </remarks>
    private string Said => _seat?.Seating switch
    {
        SeatingOpinion.Ask => "You have asked the table to change seats. It happens before the next deal unless somebody would rather not.",
        SeatingOpinion.Refuse => "You would rather the seats stayed as they are. Nobody else's asking can move them.",
        _ => "The seats stay as they are until somebody asks and nobody minds."
    };

    /// <remarks>
    /// ⚠️ Unhooking, and nothing else — <c>StateHasChanged</c> must never be called from here,
    /// because disposal can run during renderer teardown. <b>The seat itself is not disposed
    /// here</b>: it belongs to whoever sat down, which is the island above this one (P13.6).
    /// </remarks>
    public void Dispose() => Unhook();

    private void Unhook()
    {
        if (_seat is not null)
        {
            _seat.Changed -= OnAsked;
        }
    }
}
